<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 28 November, from 936 to 1943.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/shi-jingtang" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shi-jingtang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/936">936 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,090 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Shi Jingtang is enthroned as first emperor of the Later Jin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yelu-deguang">Yelü Deguang</a> enthroned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-jingtang">Shi Jingtang</a>, who had rebelled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiyuan">Taiyuan</a> against the Later Tang, as founding emperor of the Later Jin. In return Shi ceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixteen-prefectures">Sixteen Prefectures</a> and called himself the son of the Liao emperor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-jingtang">Shi Jingtang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yelu-deguang">Yelü Deguang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-congke">Li Congke</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1443">1443 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">583 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Skanderbeg takes Krujë with a forged letter from the sultan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having deserted the Ottoman army, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a> and, using a forged letter from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> to its governor, became lord of the city. Its castle became his stronghold in twenty-five years of resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1470">1470 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">556 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lê Thánh Tông sets out by sea to attack Champa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-thanh-tong">Lê Thánh Tông</a> of Đại Việt led a 100,000-strong naval expedition from Hóa Châu against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>, in retaliation for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> raids. In 1471 he captured Vijaya, the Cham capital, in a war widely seen as marking Champa's downfall.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-thanh-tong">Lê Thánh Tông</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1520">1520 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">506 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Magellan's ships enter the Pacific</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After 38 days navigating the strait at the tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan</a>'s three remaining ships reached the open ocean. He named it the Pacific for its calm waters.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1666">1666 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">360 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royal forces defeat Covenanter insurgents at Rullion Green</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At least 3,000 men of the Scots Army under Tam Dalyell of the Binns defeated about 900 Covenanter insurgents led by James Wallace of Auchens at Rullion Green. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/covenanters">Covenanters</a>, Scottish Presbyterians, were persecuted after the Restoration.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/covenanters">Covenanters</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arthur Griffith launches Sinn Féin's policy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a convention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, Arthur Griffith set out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinn-fein">Sinn Féin</a> policy, meaning 'we ourselves', of Irish self-reliance and a separate Irish parliament. The movement later became central to the struggle for independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albania declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Vlorë</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-qemali">Ismail Qemali</a> raised the Albanian flag and proclaimed independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>. The great powers recognised the new state the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Churchill, Roosevelt and Stalin meet in Tehran</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 'Big Three' met together for the first time at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> Conference. They committed to a cross-Channel invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1944 and discussed the shape of post-war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 28 November <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-i-komnenos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-i-komnenos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel I Komnenos</span><span class="tp">1118–1180</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-tudor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-tudor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret Tudor</span><span class="tp">1489–1541</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-blake"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-blake.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Blake</span><span class="tp">1757–1827</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-xii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso XII</span><span class="tp">1857–1885</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ernst-rohm"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ernst-rohm.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ernst Röhm</span><span class="tp">1887–1934</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 28 November <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/owain-gwynedd"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/owain-gwynedd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Owain Gwynedd</span><span class="tp">c. 1100–1170</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eleanor-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eleanor of Castile</span><span class="tp">1241–1290</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gian-lorenzo-bernini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gian-lorenzo-bernini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gian Lorenzo Bernini</span><span class="tp">1598–1680</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-de-buade-de-frontenac"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-de-buade-de-frontenac.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis de Buade de Frontenac</span><span class="tp">1622–1698</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philippe-leclerc-de-hauteclocque"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippe-leclerc-de-hauteclocque.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philippe Leclerc de Hauteclocque</span><span class="tp">1902–1947</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/enrico-fermi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enrico-fermi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Enrico Fermi</span><span class="tp">1901–1954</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wilhelmina-of-the-netherlands"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wilhelmina-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wilhelmina of the Netherlands</span><span class="tp">1880–1962</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
